Properties.Value:
{%- comment -%}
  One wording, sized for SMS, sent unchanged on push, SMS and email, so
  nobody gets a worse version because of the channel they prefer.
  Measured: failed 63-95 chars, slow 114, test 102. All one SMS.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign printerName = Workflow | Attribute:'PrinterName' -%}
{%- assign eventKind = Workflow | Attribute:'event' -%}
{%- assign reason = Workflow | Attribute:'reason' -%}
{%- assign printersFailing = Workflow | Attribute:'printersFailing' | AsInteger -%}
{%- assign elapsedMs = Workflow | Attribute:'elapsedMs' | AsInteger -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Time comes from 'Now', NOT from occurredAt. Deliberate: occurredAt is UTC
  with a Z and NOTHING in Lava converts it - Date, Date with a timezone
  argument, ToLocalTime and AsDateTime all ignore the Z, so 14:15Z reads as
  2:15pm instead of 9:15am. Rock's 'Now' is already org time, and the proxy
  posts within a second of the failure with no retry.
  Do not change this back to occurredAt. It puts every message 5-6 hours out
  and it looks correct in a template review.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign whenText = 'Now' | Date:'h:mmtt' | Downcase -%}

{%- comment -%} Scope clause only when more than one printer is down. "0 other printers" is noise. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign othersText = '' -%}
{%- if printersFailing > 1 -%}
{%- assign otherCount = printersFailing | Minus:1 -%}
{%- assign othersText = ' ' | Append:otherCount | Append:' other printers also failing.' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if eventKind == 'slow' -%}
{%- assign seconds = elapsedMs | DividedBy:1000.0 | Format:'0.0' -%}
Check-in printer {{ printerName }} was slow ({{ seconds }}s) - check-in showed a timeout but the label may have printed. {{ whenText }}
{%- elseif eventKind == 'test' -%}
TEST from the cloud print proxy - no printer is broken. Sent to prove notifications reach you. {{ whenText }}
{%- else -%}
Check-in printer {{ printerName }} failed: {{ reason }}.{{ othersText }} {{ whenText }}
{%- endif -%}

