Properties.Value:
{%- comment -%}
  One channel for this person. A device that can actually receive a push
  wins; otherwise their own communication preference.

  Writes exactly push, sms or email - the three send steps below are each
  gated on this value, so exactly one of them applies.

  TRAP: DeviceRegistrationId CANNOT be filtered in where:. Both
  != null and != '' return the unnarrowed result. One real person here
  has 20 devices with notifications enabled, 6 active, and only 5 that
  carry a registration id - so the obvious filter overcounts and routes
  people to a channel that cannot reach them. Check it in the loop.

  CommunicationPreference renders as a NAME but filters as an integer:
  0 RecipientPreference, 1 Email, 2 SMS, 3 PushNotification. Compared
  against the rendered name here on purpose.

  REQUIRES Enabled Lava Commands: RockEntity
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign recipient = Activity | Attribute:'Recipient','Object' -%}
{%- assign aliasId = recipient.PrimaryAlias.Id | AsInteger -%}
{%- assign preference = recipient.CommunicationPreference -%}
{%- assign pushable = 0 -%}
{%- if aliasId > 0 -%}
    {% personaldevice where:'PersonAliasId == {{ aliasId }} && NotificationsEnabled == true && IsActive == true' limit:'25' %}
        {%- for d in personaldeviceItems -%}
            {%- if d.DeviceRegistrationId != null and d.DeviceRegistrationId != '' -%}
                {%- assign pushable = pushable | Plus:1 -%}
                {% break %}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
    {% endpersonaldevice %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if pushable > 0 -%}push{%- elseif preference == 'SMS' -%}sms{%- else -%}email{%- endif -%}

